{
  "case_id": "2022-22-96",
  "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2016, Congress passed the Puerto Rico Oversight, Management, and Economic Stability Act (PROMESA), 48 U. S. C. \u00a7 2101 et seq., to deal with a fscal crisis in Puerto Rico brought about by soaring public debt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When CPI's requests went unfulflled, it sued the Board in the United States District Court for Puerto Rico, citing a provision of the Puerto Rican Constitution interpreted to guarantee a right of access to public records."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Centro de Periodismo Investigativo, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CPI claims to identify the required clear statement in PROMESA's establishment of a judicial review scheme. Section 2126(a) provides that \u201cany action against the Oversight Board, and any action otherwise arising out of\u201d PROMESA, \u201cshall be brought\u201d in the Federal District Court for Puerto Rico."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We hold it does not. Under long-settled law, Congress must use unmistakable language to abrogate sovereign immunity. Nothing in the statute creating the board meets that high bar."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CPI",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CPI contends we can still find a clear statement in PROMESA, based on the statute's establishment of a judicial review scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "this Court has held, validly abrogates the immunity of \u201cgovernments\u201d and \u201cgovernmental agencies\u201d from all actions it authorizes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So PROMESA's judicial review scheme\u2014absent a categorical abrogation of immunity\u2014still has plenty of work to do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-22-96",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98faec7b5e5d03104853ddbfbe548cdc29fc0199a2c9db15d17567789cef21ef",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98faec7b5e5d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "United States has urged us to hold that Puerto Rico enjoys a form of common-law immunity that, it claims, territorial governments can invoke in federal court."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
